{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"asbestos-popular-tench","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe RCA for grindable-deviant-angwantibo proved that any captured nested pytest without a private `--basetemp` joins pytest's user-global numbered root and synchronously performs unrelated stale-tree cleanup at session finish. The original helper is fixed in that ticket, but the required construct sweep found five semantically confirmed sibling launch sites outside its caller path.\n\n## Confirmed sibling sites\n- tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py:163-177\n- tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:830-844\n- tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py:183-204\n- tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py:154-178\n- tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py:92-116\n\nThe already-safe precedents are tests/unit/test_external_isolation.py:64-76 and tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py:14-25, which pass a private basetemp derived from parent-owned temporary state.\n\n## Plan\n- Inventory every live nested pytest subprocess and classify whether it already owns a private basetemp.\n- Give each confirmed sibling a unique parent-owned basetemp without changing its entrypoint, cwd, marker selection, or child assertions.\n- Add behavior-level regression coverage using an isolated cleanup-eligible `PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT`; avoid timing and source-text oracles.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every live nested pytest subprocess owns a unique parent-scoped basetemp or has a cited reason shared retention is required.\n- [ ] A real-subprocess test proves cleanup-eligible shared numbered-tree sentinels remain byte-for-byte untouched.\n- [ ] Existing entrypoint/cwd/selection contracts for all five sibling tests still pass.\n- [ ] The default unit suite and lint/typecheck gates pass.","id":"fb03-2609-ef83-4b41","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["test-isolation","flaky"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Nested pytest meta-tests still clean the user-global numbered temp root"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786891938793583001,"uuid":"d32811a2-cdb9-45e4-be32-4bb347c28870"}